codex
The proof is non-vacuous and body-sensitive: a fresh odd-result `+1` mutation exits 1 with the expected stuck equality, and changing the executed even body while keeping its postcondition also exits 1 with a residual distinguishing the two result terms. The decisive failures are therefore not “the prover accepted anything”; they are that the proved program/formula is the wrong even-case algorithm, the claims exclude valid length-two and non-integer numeric inputs, and the proof-local result abstraction lacks an independent connection theorem. I’m consolidating those findings and the full 937-record rule assessment into `REVIEW.md`.
